<title>USA: Sallie Mae Q4 net, shr rise.</title>
<headline>Sallie Mae Q4 net, shr rise.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON, D.C. 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>1996			1995</p>
<p> Shr			  $2.01		    $1.67</p>
<p> Net			112,288		  102,896</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  54,485		   59,862</p>
<p>	  12 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $7.32		    $5.27</p>
<p> Net			419,410		  366,279</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  55,811		   67,451</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTES: Q4 1996 includes one-time after-tax gain of $5.8 million or $0.10 per share for successful outcome of lawsuit regarding special allowance payments on certain loan categories.</p>
<p>Core net income (earnings net of recognized floor revenues) for Q4 1996 was $107.1 million or $1.92 per share, up from $97.8 million or $1.59 per share for 1995 Q4.</p>
</text>
